closing arguments in jesse smallett's  criminal trial are set to start later  this morning the former empire actor was  seen outside the courtroom yesterday  before finishing his second day of  testimony smallett again denied staging  a racist anti-gay attack on himself back  in january 2019. charlie damar is  covering this trial  returning to the stand tuesday jesse  smilet faced heated cross-examination by  prosecutors who wanted to know more  about his interactions with the two men  they say helped him stage an alleged  fake attack when asked about video of  him picking up abel and ola osindaro in  his car just days before the attack  smellet denied recruiting the brothers  to stage a hoax  simolette admitted that he drove past  the location where the alleged attack  would occur several times with both  those and darrell's in the car the actor  said there was nothing unusual about  them just driving around smilet was also  pressed about private social media  messages from the night of the reported  attack updating the brothers on the  status of his delayed flight and a call  from abel osendaro after he landed  osindaro testified that the call was to  confirm the time of the fake attack  smilet denied that ever happened on  tuesday  the jury is expected to get the case  today after closing arguments and will  determine if the 39-year-old is guilty  of six felony counts of disorderly  conduct for cbs morning's charlie demar  in chicago
 

